# patches/rk3588-topeet/linux/series — board patches for rk3588-topeet (mainline v7.1 base).
# One patch filename per line (quilt style); '#' = comment, blank lines OK.
# Applied by forge's PatchApplier (git am --3way --signoff, bisectable) onto the
# pinned v7.1 tag; forge skips apply only on a series-content fingerprint match.
#
# 0001 — OOT DRM panel driver (panel-topeet-dsi.c) that replays the vendor
#        panel-init-sequence / panel-exit-sequence byte blobs (Rockchip BSP
#        "simple-panel-dsi" binding). For the 10.1" 1024x600 DSI->LVDS bridge
#        panel, whose bridge IC has no mainline driver. + Kconfig/Makefile.
# 0002 — the rk3588-topeet board DT: Phase 1 boot essentials (eMMC/GMAC/USB/
#        PMIC rk806/CPU supplies) + Phase 3 display pipeline (VOP2 vp2 -> dsi0
#        mipi-dsi2 -> panel on mipidcphy0 + pwm-backlight + vcc3v3_lcd_n) +
#        Goodix GT911 touch on i2c2 + vendor-compatible ttyFIQ0 ownership of
#        UART2. + Makefile dtb-y wiring. Supersedes the
#        formerly-in-tree DT (kills the re-fetch reproducibility debt).
# 0003 — complete Rockchip vendor FIQ debugger/ttyFIQ0 stack ported from the
#        5.10 SDK to Linux 7.1, including the RK UART backend and TrustZone SiP
#        ABI adapter. UART2 remains disabled for serial8250 and is never ttyS2.
# 0004 — Rockchip vendor RK860X regulator driver plus the focused RK3x I2C
#        SCL-hold timeout recovery/reset path. RK8602/RK8603 are no longer
#        claimed by the generic FAN53555 driver.
# 0005 — release the Goodix GT911 reset line after its I2C address-selection
#        window, matching both vendor Goodix implementations on this board.
# 0006 — bind GT911 power/probe ordering to the integrated LCD module and
#        preserve the vendor 20 ms post-supply stabilization interval.
# 0009 — preserve the RK3588 vendor VOP hardware handoff in mainline: ACLK
#        750 MHz, VP2 parented from V0PLL, and per-VP DCLK reset after timing
#        commit. This targets the vblank timeouts preceding the hard lock.
# 0011 — port the RK3588 vendor CPU DVFS transaction to Linux 7.1 OPP
#        callbacks: dual cpu/mem rails, intermediate SCMI rates, SRAM read
#        margins, rollback and big-core cpuidle coordination.
# 0012 — fix 0011's registration: cluster bring-up moved from a bare
#        module_init (which permanently died on -EPROBE_DEFER at 1.133s, 8ms
#        before the SCMI transport appeared — CPUFreq never ran since 0011)
#        into a platform-driver probe with proper deferral retry; also ports
#        the vendor panic notifier dumping each cluster's last freq/volt.
#        With this the ramoops window moved 0x110000 -> 0x10000000 in 0002
#        (the low window is cleared by the mainline TPL/ddrbin boot chain).
# 0013-0017 — upstream (v7.2) race hardening, not hang fixes: schedutil
#        sg_cpu publication (f0a3f042293a), OPP add/lookup kref
#        (f5e1cc9a284b), and the rtw88 trio incl. the 8723du-relevant TX
#        report timeout (c80788f7c, 6b964941b, aa7d92e83).
# 0020 — cluster AFBC modifier lists split per SoC (modifier tables are SoC
#        hardware capability tables; rk3576 already had its own — the
#        rk3568/rk3588 sharing let RK3588 silently inherit RK3568's genuine
#        AFBC-only restriction). rk3568 keeps AFBC-only (its check rejects
#        LINEAR); rk3588 appends LINEAR after the nine AFBC variants, priority
#        preserved — mod_supported() already accepts LINEAR on every RK3588
#        window, but the AFBC-only IN_FORMATS blob made modifier-negotiating
#        clients with a software renderer (sim/llvmpipe) fail GBM allocation
#        with EGL_BAD_ALLOC. Found in sim campaign 4 (mutter
#        lock_front_buffer failure).
# 0007/0008 were a coupled I2C-v5 + GT911 polling experiment. Candidate
#        c670a208... did not reach login reliably, so both are intentionally
#        excluded below. Keep the patch files only as failed-test evidence.
#
# NOTE: rk3588 dsi0 = "rk3588-mipi-dsi2" controller → kernel.config enables
# CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_DW_MIPI_DSI2 (NOT _DSI). PHY label is mipidcphy0.

